# NOTE ON SYNTAX, learned 2026-09-06: a `#` starts a comment ONLY at the start of a line.
# Trailing text after a pattern is PART OF THE PATTERN, so `*.old   # backup` is a rule that
# matches a file literally named that and therefore matches nothing. Two rules here were
# written that way and had been inert since they were added — `*.st` and `*.old` — found when
# `pcal.trans` left a Revoke.old that showed up as untracked despite an apparent rule for it.
# Comments go on their own line. Verify a new rule with `git check-ignore -v <path>` rather
# than by reading it: an ignore rule that does nothing looks exactly like one that works.
#
# Toolchain binaries — never commit jars/binaries; document how to fetch them instead
tla2tools.jar
*.jar
tla/toolbox-state/
tla/states/
# TLC state dumps
*.st
MC.out

